
# Diagnostic renders. Every one of these scripts is versioned along with the
# report it writes; the frames themselves are evidence for one investigation
# and are regenerated by re-running the script.
#
# The reports stay in the repository deliberately. tools/effect_probe_report.txt
# in particular is the ground truth tools/index_audit.js checks every indexed
# property write against, so losing it would turn a real audit into a skipped
# one.
tools/contact_sheet.png
tools/bisect/
tools/reach/
tools/fluid_lab_*.png

# Card renders are NOT ignored. tools/render_cards.jsx writes css/previews/ and
# those ship in the package — they are product assets, not diagnostics.

# Build output. tools/build.ps1 regenerates both from source.
build/
dist/

# The signing certificate and its password never go in the repository.
# Losing it means future updates are signed by a different identity and read
# as a different product to the installer, so keep it somewhere safe —
# just not here.
tools/certificate.p12
tools/ZXPSignCmd*.exe

# Editor and OS litter
*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The certificate password, if -NewCert wrote it out. Move it to a password
# manager and delete the file.
tools/certificate-password.txt

# OpenSSL's random seed file, dropped in the working directory by certificate
# generation. Regenerated on demand and meaningless to anyone else.
.rnd
